## STEP 15 — SELF-HOSTED RUNNER (for corporate apps)

If the target website is internal/behind VPN, GitHub's hosted runners
(on Azure) cannot reach it. Solution: self-hosted runner on your machine.

```powershell
# Create runner folder
mkdir C:\actions-runner
cd C:\actions-runner

# Follow instructions from:
# Repo → Settings → Actions → Runners → New self-hosted runner
# Copy and run the commands GitHub shows you

# Start the runner
.\run.cmd
```

Then change one line in `playwright.yml`:
```yaml
# Change this:
runs-on: ubuntu-latest

# To this:
runs-on: self-hosted
```

Now GitHub sends jobs to YOUR machine which is inside the network.

